# SBMM storm-structure survey — the intake js/pipes.js is waiting for
# (docs/V19_HYDRO3_SPEC.md §3). Copy to data/storm_survey.csv, fill in what was
# surveyed, leave the rest blank, then:  python tools/build_storm_network.py
#
# node_id      a node id from data/storm_network.json (a conduit id also works,
#              for diameter_in / material / status)
# invert_ft    the surveyed pipe invert at that structure, NAVD88 ft
# rim_ft       the surveyed rim/grate elevation, NAVD88 ft (blank = the lidar
#              ground the app already computes on boot)
# diameter_in  the pipe's inside diameter
# material     one of: HDPE, corrugated HDPE, RCP, reinforced concrete, CMP,
#              corrugated metal  (js/pipes.js PIPE_N maps these to Manning's n)
# date, source who measured it and when — it becomes the feature's provenance
#
# A conduit gets a CAPACITY once both its ends have an invert and it has a
# diameter and a material. Until then js/pipes.js reports "unknown — survey
# pending" and names which of the three is missing; it never guesses one.
node_id,invert_ft,rim_ft,diameter_in,material,date,source
herman_pipe_n_end,,,24,corrugated HDPE,,
herman_pipe_s_end,,,24,corrugated HDPE,,
storm_main_east,,,24,,,
junction,,,24,,,
outfall,,,24,,,
spot_8,,,,,,
